        "explanationEn": "The correct Sanskrit verse of Shloka 288 is «एतच्छास्त्रानुसारेण यः प्रीत्या श्रद्धया जनः। आज्ञोपासनयोर्दार्ढ्यं प्रकुर्यात् स्वस्य जीवने॥».\nMeaning: Those who faithfully and lovingly strengthen āgnā and upāsanā in their life according to this shastra earn the pleasure of Bhagwan and become a recipient of his grace. While living, they attain the brāhmi sthiti described in the shastras. They master ekāntik dharma . They attain the eternal and divine Akshardham of Bhagwan, ultimate moksha and bliss. (288–290)",
        "fullSanskritDevanagari": "एतच्छास्त्रानुसारेण यः प्रीत्या श्रद्धया जनः।\nआज्ञोपासनयोर्दार्ढ्यं प्रकुर्यात् स्वस्य जीवने॥ २८८॥",
